# What may enter a Docker build context. Used by apps/web/Dockerfile and apps/cms/Dockerfile,
# which build from the repository root. The aim: no secret, no local data and no git history
# can reach an image, even by a careless COPY.
#
# Rules are read top to bottom and the last one that matches wins.

# 1. Nothing enters unless it is listed in section 2.
*

# 2. The files the builds need.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/web
!apps/cms
!packages/shared

# 3. Even inside those folders, these never enter. Because they come last they beat section 2.
# Real settings and keys (an .env.example is an example, and nothing builds from it).
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/keys
# Version control and the work files of this repository.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.gitattributes
**/.superpowers
# Installed and generated files: the build makes its own inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.astro
**/.strapi
**/.strapi-updater.json
**/.tmp
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Tests and their output.
**/*.test.*
**/*.spec.*
**/tests
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage
# Local data: databases, dumps, uploads, logs.
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
**/*.sql
**/*.log
apps/cms/public/uploads
apps/cms/exports
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
